.TH OBSIDIAN-INSTALLER 1 "September 2026" "obsidian-installer 0.1.0"
.SH NAME
obsidian-installer \- verified official Obsidian application delivery
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B obsidian-installer install --assumeyes
.br
.B obsidian-installer update --assumeyes
.br
.B obsidian-installer release --json
.br
.B obsidian-installer prepare --directory DIR
.RB [ --app-version " VERSION"]
.br
.B obsidian-installer apply --appimage FILE --sha256 HEX --app-version VERSION --assumeyes
.br
.B obsidian-installer status --json
.br
.B obsidian-installer uninstall --assumeyes
.SH DESCRIPTION
Installing or upgrading the helper RPM queues a one-shot systemd job after
DNF finishes. It downloads the package-selected official AppImage, verifies
its SHA-256 and identity, extracts it and creates desktop integration.
COPR contains only the helper. Check systemctl status obsidian-installer.service
and journalctl -u obsidian-installer.service for completion or failure.
The job retries failed operations, up to three starts in 15 minutes.
Reinstalling the RPM queues another attempt.
.PP
New helper releases update the AppImage and its bundled Electron runtime.
Obsidian's own application updates remain available. The helper does not
modify user settings, vaults or existing Flatpak installations.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B install, update
Require root and --assumeyes. Reconcile the package-selected release.
Reject changed or foreign files, metadata drift and downgrades. Repair
missing known desktop links from the retained verified artifact offline.
.TP
.B prepare
Download a stable official release into the requested existing directory
without installing it. With no version, use the official desktop release feed.
Print the artifact path, version, source and SHA-256 as JSON.
.TP
.B apply
Require root and explicit --appimage, --sha256, --app-version and --assumeyes.
Verify the artifact and ownership before replacing the application bundle.
.TP
.B release, status
Read-only JSON output. Release prints the packaged selection without network
access. Status verifies existing installation and ownership, including any
interrupted removal. Unknown state is an error.
.TP
.B uninstall
Require root and --assumeyes. Remove only verified owned application files
and desktop integration. Preserve vaults and all user configuration.
Interrupted removal can be retried; changed or foreign files block removal.
Final RPM removal invokes this command automatically.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /opt/obsidian/
AppImage, extracted application, launcher, desktop entry and receipt.
.TP
.B /usr/local/bin/obsidian
Application launch command.
.TP
.B /usr/local/share/applications/obsidian.desktop
Desktop integration, including obsidian:// links.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates success. Nonzero indicates an invalid request, failed
verification, unsupported platform or incomplete operation.
